y, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as a know-it-all, has a hot temper.\n\nWe need to evaluate criteria: reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, decision quality, attention, crew cooperation, communication, responsibility, adaptability.\n\nLet's assess each:\n\nA: strong technical (anticipate dangerous, complex connections, spatial vision), leadership. But show-off, not open to new ideas => concerns on cooperation, adaptability. No info on stress resilience, reliability, communication.\n\nB: very conscientious (reliability), handles stress well (stress resilience), good weather assessment (technical), excellent computer skills (technical). Weak memory for numbers (attention), makes nasty remarks (crew cooperation, communication). So strong reliability but poor teamwork.\n\nC: quick correct decisions (decision quality), keeps calm in crisis (stress), understands complicated tech (technical), but difficulty communicating, egocentric, not willing to further education (adaptability). So good decision and stress but poor cooperation.\n\nD: responds adequately to unexpected (stress), concentrates well (attention), solves problems extremely well (technical), takes responsibility seriously (responsibility), but hot temper (crew cooperation), know-it-all (openness). So mixed.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. All have some concerns. Which candidate has strongest overall? B has strong reliability and stress, but nasty remarks is serious for crew cooperation. C has good decision and calm but communication issues. D has good problem solving and responsibility but hot temper. A has technical but show-off and not open.\n\nProbably none perfect. Which has least severe concerns? B's nasty remarks could be severe for crew environment. C's communication difficulty and egocentric also severe. D's hot temper also severe. A's show-off and not open to new ideas also problematic.\n\nWe might need to ask other panel members for missing info, e.g., about stress resilience for A, reliability for C, etc. But we need to make a contribution now. Perhaps start by highlighting Candidate B's strengths and concerns, and ask others about their view on his teamwork.\n\nWe need to state current recommendation. Could say currently leaning towards Candidate B due to strong reliability and stress handling, but need clarification on crew cooperation.\n\nThus vote for B.\n\nLet's produce public message with vote B."}
